477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 356 0 R
/E (History demonstrates that the most profound scientific breakthroughs rarely offer clean solutions, but instead solve critical limitations of their era, and in turn uncover a new, often vastly more complex problem in their wake. For example, the Industrial Revolution led to a reduction in the need for manual labour through mechanisation, but brought about unprecedented environmental issues and degradation we are still grappling with today. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
478 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 356 0 R
/E (Today, Artificial Intelligence is driving a similar paradox within the mathematical and scientific community. Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) refers to computer systems designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence. These tasks include understanding spoken language, recognizing images, making decisions, and generating new content like text or art, or even solving complex problems. This ability, so humanlike yet so alien in the immense processing capabilities, has been a source of controversy within the mathematical community. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
