/T (This tension is clearest in recent AI breakthroughs involving the Navier-Stokes equations, one of the seven famous Millennium Prize Problems. These equations describe how fluids like air and water move, governing everything from climate patterns to turbulence around aeroplane wings. Because fluid motion is so chaotic, mathematicians have struggled to solve them for over two hundred years. Recently, swarms of AI agents operating autonomously have begun finding new patterns and potential solutions that humans missed. Unlike the 1976 supercomputer, which simply checked a list of maps built by humans, modern AI creates its own logical paths across high-dimensional spaces that human brains may struggle to visualise. )
/E (This tension is clearest in recent AI breakthroughs involving the Navier-Stokes equations, one of the seven famous Millennium Prize Problems. These equations describe how fluids like air and water move, governing everything from climate patterns to turbulence around aeroplane wings. Because fluid motion is so chaotic, mathematicians have struggled to solve them for over two hundred years. Recently, swarms of AI agents operating autonomously have begun finding new patterns and potential solutions that humans missed. Unlike the 1976 supercomputer, which simply checked a list of maps built by humans, modern AI creates its own logical paths across high-dimensional spaces that human brains may struggle to visualise. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
