/T (When a model solves a centuries-old equation, the milestone is often packaged as a marketing showcase to attract investors and showcase processing power, rather than published as a collaborative tool designed for the broader academic community to learn from. Furthermore, this commercial race creates a rather unbalanced environment where elite tech companies hold the exclusive hardware resources needed to run multi-agent swarms, leaving public universities and independent researchers sidelined. If high-level problem-solving becomes concentrated behind proprietary corporate models, the open, democratic nature of scientific discovery is replaced by a closed ecosystem possibly driven by profit margins and proprietary benchmarks rather than the collective advancement of human knowledge.)
