/T (133 hours into the flight, re-entry preparations had to begin. The CM and navigational computer had to be turned back on after a complete shutdown. Furthermore it had to be done with the reduced power output of the fuel cell. Tests on the ground were run for the past few days to see the optimal way to power on and the sequence was relayed to the crew. After startup it was clear that there was an issue. All the computers on the ground had been operating under the assumption that the crew would have brought back a couple of tonnes of moon rocks with them. Since they never landed, they were underweight and their trajectory was slightly off.)
/E (133 hours into the flight, re-entry preparations had to begin. The CM and navigational computer had to be turned back on after a complete shutdown. Furthermore it had to be done with the reduced power output of the fuel cell. Tests on the ground were run for the past few days to see the optimal way to power on and the sequence was relayed to the crew. After startup it was clear that there was an issue. All the computers on the ground had been operating under the assumption that the crew would have brought back a couple of tonnes of moon rocks with them. Since they never landed, they were underweight and their trajectory was slightly off.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
