/T (None of the crew ever flew in space again, Jim Lovel, the commander, retired in 1973 and passed away in August 2025. Fred Haise, after recovering from his urinary tract infection, was planned to go on a later Apollo mission which was unfortunately cancelled due to budget cuts from Congress, he went on to work on the space shuttle programme before leaving NASA to pursue Aerospace full time, currently the only living crew-member as of September 2026. Jack Swigert left NASA in 1977, going into politics and later elected to join the House of Representatives but passing away from bone cancer in 1982 before he went into office.)
/E (None of the crew ever flew in space again, Jim Lovel, the commander, retired in 1973 and passed away in August 2025. Fred Haise, after recovering from his urinary tract infection, was planned to go on a later Apollo mission which was unfortunately cancelled due to budget cuts from Congress, he went on to work on the space shuttle programme before leaving NASA to pursue Aerospace full time, currently the only living crew-member as of September 2026. Jack Swigert left NASA in 1977, going into politics and later elected to join the House of Representatives but passing away from bone cancer in 1982 before he went into office.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
