623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 372 0 R
/T (What makes this even more interesting is that the irrigation itself was inefficient. This was mainly due to the irrigation infrastructure, which was inefficient. Water was lost through leakage from canals, seepage into the surrounding soils, and evaporation. Additionally, poor drainage also created other problems. Soil salinity also started becoming concerning. In an arid environment, irrigation water contains dissolved salts. )
/E (What makes this even more interesting is that the irrigation itself was inefficient. This was mainly due to the irrigation infrastructure, which was inefficient. Water was lost through leakage from canals, seepage into the surrounding soils, and evaporation. Additionally, poor drainage also created other problems. Soil salinity also started becoming concerning. In an arid environment, irrigation water contains dissolved salts. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 372 0 R
/T (When plants use some of the water and the rest evaporates, it leaves salts in the soil, making it saline and unsuitable for crops to grow in. Although the system was designed to keep agricultural productivity growing, it became a reason for its loss on a huge scale. Later, the Aral Sea started to shrink in volume dramatically. This increased the salinity of the sea and contributed to the loss of many aquatic animals, such as the Aral barbel and Aral nase. )
/E (When plants use some of the water and the rest evaporates, it leaves salts in the soil, making it saline and unsuitable for crops to grow in. Although the system was designed to keep agricultural productivity growing, it became a reason for its loss on a huge scale. Later, the Aral Sea started to shrink in volume dramatically. This increased the salinity of the sea and contributed to the loss of many aquatic animals, such as the Aral barbel and Aral nase. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
