/E (That accidental spill opened the door to new research on artificial sweeteners. Saccharin turned out to be roughly 300 times sweeter than regular cane sugar, yet it carried zero calories \(National Cancer Institute, 2023; Hicks, 2010\). Over the next century, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration \(FDA\) would go on to approve several other zero-calorie sugar substitutes, including aspartame, sucralose, and acesulfame potassium \(U.S. Food and Drug Administration, 2023\).)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
