/Title (In traditional baking and cooking, real sugar does a lot more than just make items taste good. It adds bulk, texture, moisture, and structure to food. When you take sugar out, the food looks and tastes pretty unappealing. High-intensity sweeteners offered a sneaky workaround: manufacturers could use cheap chemical fillers, water, and industrial emulsifiers to rebuild the food's structure, and then add a tiny pinch of artificial sweetener to fix the flavor \(Seto et al., 2025, p. 2\).)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3130 0 R
/First 3131 0 R
/Last 3131 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 3122 0 R
>>
endobj
