/Title (On September 8, 2026, OpenAI announced that a network of 10,000 autonomous AI agents running for 88 hours produced a 166-page proof claiming to solve the Navier-Stokes existence and smoothness problem by demonstrating the formation of a mathematical singularity, where the fluid reaches infinite speed in finite time with no energy change possible in the mathematical model, despite this not being able to occur in reality due to fluid viscosity, showing a critical breakdown in the model.)
