3150 0 obj
<<
/Title (When a model solves a centuries-old equation, the milestone is often packaged as a marketing showcase to attract investors and showcase processing power, rather than published as a collaborative tool designed for the broader academic community to learn from. Furthermore, this commercial race creates a rather unbalanced environment where elite tech companies hold the exclusive hardware resources needed to run multi-agent swarms, leaving public universities and independent researchers sidelined. If high-level problem-solving becomes concentrated behind proprietary corporate models, the open, democratic nature of scientific discovery is replaced by a closed ecosystem possibly driven by profit margins and proprietary benchmarks rather than the collective advancement of human knowledge.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3148 0 R
/Next 3152 0 R
>>
endobj
3151 0 obj
<<
/Title (In Nigeria, nearly half of communities in the Niger Delta receive fewer than two hours of electricity per day, despite being connected to the regional power grid \(Stakeholder Democracy Network, 2016\). Beyond the Delta, the problem is even more widespread: the Nigerian government estimates that more than 80 million people nationwide lack reliable access to electricity \(Stakeholder Democracy Network, 2016\). As a result, many households rely on kerosene lamps, diesel generators, and wood fires for light and energy, all of which release pollutants and increase the risk of respiratory illness.)
