<<
/Title (When plants use some of the water and the rest evaporates, it leaves salts in the soil, making it saline and unsuitable for crops to grow in. Although the system was designed to keep agricultural productivity growing, it became a reason for its loss on a huge scale. Later, the Aral Sea started to shrink in volume dramatically. This increased the salinity of the sea and contributed to the loss of many aquatic animals, such as the Aral barbel and Aral nase.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3173 0 R
/Next 3167 0 R
>>
endobj
3172 0 obj
<<
/Title (SC: Yeah, we got a main bus A under volt now to sh owin g.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3170 0 R
/Next 3174 0 R
>>
endobj
3173 0 obj
<<
/Title (What makes this even more interesting is that the irrigation itself was inefficient. This was mainly due to the irrigation infrastructure, which was inefficient. Water was lost through leakage from canals, seepage into the surrounding soils, and evaporation. Additionally, poor drainage also created other problems. Soil salinity also started becoming concerning. In an arid environment, irrigation water contains dissolved salts.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3175 0 R
/Next 3171 0 R
>>
endobj
3174 0 obj
<<
/Title (CAP COM: Main A under volt.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3172 0 R
/Next 3176 0 R
>>
endobj
3175 0 obj
<<
/Title (The 1960s was the main turning point for the project planned by the Soviets. It was an age of intensification of the irrigation project and cotton production. This converted vast areas of Central Asia into farmland. Studies made by the FAO also indicate that irrigated land increased from 4.5 million hectares to 7 million hectares between 1960 and 1980. At this point, the consequences became easily visible when the water volume in the Aral Sea started decreasing. Since the two main rivers of the region had their water redirected away from the sea, there was significantly less water flowing into the Aral Sea. With the contribution of the very dry climate in the region and the irrigation project, the water in the sea started to evaporate, causing it to become much smaller than before.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3177 0 R
/Next 3173 0 R
>>
endobj
